explanation:
The body takes the library's matrix special isogeny `TauCeti.specialIsogeny` on the standard symplectic matrix group and moves it to the pinned scheme points along the group isomorphism `pinnedEquivSymplectic`, as e⁻¹ ∘ τ ∘ e. The composition runs in the right direction. Moving a map along an isomorphism in this way is the standard way to define the same endomorphism on an isomorphic model of the group.

The file goes on to prove the expected properties:
- the two equivalences intertwine the maps (`pinnedEquivSymplectic_pinnedHalfFrobenius`, `carrierEquivPinned_halfFrobenius`);
- its square is the prime-field Frobenius;
- it swaps the long and short simple root subgroups, raising the parameter to the right exponents (1 at the long root, 2 at the short one).

These are exactly the defining features of the half-Frobenius in Carter §12.3 and Steinberg §11. The setting (Sp₄ in characteristic 2, over the Suzuki index's field) is part of what the object is, so the definition is not too narrow. Mathlib has no special isogeny of B₂/C₂.
